{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs3HnWCMMkb7hVRKVwfD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A constrained package now skips the max-release-age cutoff entirely, so `boto3==1.35.88` resolves instead of being filtered to nothing. The relevant test files pass.\n\n**The change**\n\n- `src/fromager/bootstrap_requirement_resolver.py`: before calling `find_all_matching_from_provider`, the source-resolution path checks `self.ctx.constraints.get_constraint(req.name)`. If there is a constraint, the age cutoff is `None`. Otherwise the cutoff is computed as before. The provider still enforces the constraint itself (`is_satisfied_by` in `resolver.py`), so the pin is kept, and the misleading \"keeping all to avoid empty resolution\" warning no longer fires for pinned packages.\n- `tests/test_bootstrap_requirement_resolver_multiple.py`: added two tests.\n  - `test_resolve_constrained_package_skips_max_release_age` checks that a constrained package reaches the provider with `max_age_cutoff=None`. This is the regression test.\n  - `test_resolve_unconstrained_package_applies_max_release_age` checks that unconstrained packages still get the cutoff.\n\n**Results**\n\n- `tests/test_bootstrap_requirement_resolver_multiple.py`: 6 passed.\n- `tests/test_cooldown.py`: 36 passed.\n- I did not confirm the new regression test fails on the old code. By reading, it would, because the old code always computes a non-`None` cutoff for that call.\n- `ruff` and `mypy` are not installed in `.venv`, so I could not run the lint or type checks. Run `hatch run lint:fix` and `hatch run mypy:check` on the two files before committing.\n\n**Choices to check**\n\n- The skip applies to any constraint, not only `==` pins. A range constraint such as `boto3<2` also bypasses the age window for that package. I read the ticket's \"a constraint is explicit user intent\" as covering all constraints. If you want only exact pins to bypass the window, the check needs to look at the specifier.\n- Single-version mode is also covered, since the same branch runs there. Its fallback behavior is unchanged for unconstrained packages.\n\nNothing is committed. Say if you want a commit with the message in the project's conventional-commit format."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4069,"cache_read_input_tokens":87196,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4069},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9193a301-c12b-407a-be18-5f6874de4629","uuid":"a861fd2d-7b21-481b-bbe1-56602067e580","timestamp":"2026-10-09T17:15:13.485Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs3HnDpk175F3eJziAGC"}
